From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Open Arc Authors <dev@openarc.invalid>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 20:39:09 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] openarc: embedder: helper apps for the child processes

Replaces the unbundled openarc_helper executable with Chromium's Mac
helper model (plan C10): one app bundle per code-signing variant in
OpenArcCore.framework/Versions/A/Helpers/, named by the embedder
(openarc/app/helpers.gni, generated into openarc/app/openarc_helpers.h):

  Open Arc Helper.app             utility processes, GPU without SwiftShader
  Open Arc Helper (Renderer).app  renderers (V8 JIT)
  Open Arc Helper (GPU).app       GPU process with SwiftShader (JIT)
  Open Arc Helper (Plugin).app    reserved for library CDMs (plan C18)
  Open Arc Helper (Alerts).app    alert-style notifications

Each has an Info.plist with LSUIElement and a bundle id below
org.openarc.browser.helper (the GPU helper shares the default id, as
Chrome's does for automatic graphics switching); the app packaging
rewrites the prefix to the embedding app's id. The browser client maps
content's CHILD_NORMAL / CHILD_RENDERER / CHILD_GPU and //chrome's alerts
flag to these apps. The executable loads ../../../../OpenArcCore and
exits at once when started without --type (for example by macOS for a
notification click), as Chrome's helpers do.
